# Life 2 arrival (life/arrival.js, design/data/arrival.toml). Expect: "Arrival: x y z (grounded) ..." (271.5 y -623.5
# once grounded, about 20 s after start; a "provisional" line only on a fresh world), then a reborn bot lands within
# 3 blocks of it, on Jura's safe rim and not in Tempest, and is still alive 10 s later (area magicule there is 500;
# the forest ahead is lethal for a fresh soul). Any "ttl: ..." line is a failure. Check the biome too:
# `ttlmap 271 -624` must say ring 'rim'.
ttl arrival
ttlbot spawn TtlBotArrival
@sleep 2
kill TtlBotArrival
execute as TtlBotArrival run ttl wish knowledge
execute as TtlBotArrival run ttl choose slime
@sleep 2
ttl inspect TtlBotArrival
ttl arrival expect TtlBotArrival near 3
@sleep 10
ttl arrival expect TtlBotArrival alive
ttl arrival expect TtlBotArrival near 3
ttl reset TtlBotArrival
ttlbot remove TtlBotArrival
